## Example 1.1  


## Solve the following:  


(a) \(5.123 \times 10^{4} \mathrm{~m} + 3.28 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~m}\) (b) \(2.57 \times 10^{2} \mathrm{~mm} - 3.43 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~mm}\)  


## Solution  


(a) \(5.123 \times 10^{4} \mathrm{~mm} + 3.28 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~m} = 5.123 \times 10^{4} \mathrm{~m} + 32.8 \times 10^{4} \mathrm{~m} = (5.123 + 32.8) 10^{4} \mathrm{~m} = 37.923 \times 10^{4} \mathrm{~m} = 3.7923 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~m}\)  


(b) \(2.57 \times 10^{2} \mathrm{~mm} - 4.43 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~mm} = 2.57 \times 10^{2} \mathrm{~mm} - 0.343 \times 10^{2} \mathrm{~mm} = (2.57 - 0.343) 10^{2} \mathrm{~mm} = 2.227 \times 10^{2} \mathrm{~mm} = 2.227 \times 10^{-2} \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{~m} = 2.227 \times 10^{-5} \mathrm{~m}\)  


## Example 1.2  


Find the value of each of the following quantities:  


(a) \((4 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~kg}) (6 \times 10^{6} \mathrm{~m})\) (b) \(\frac{6 \times 10^{6} \mathrm{~m}^{3}}{2 \times 10^{2} \mathrm{~m}^{2}}\)  


## Solution  


(a) \((4 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~kg}) \left(6 \times 10^{6} \mathrm{~m}\right) = (4 \times 6) \times 10^{3} \times 10^{6} \mathrm{~kg} = 24 \times 10^{9} \mathrm{~kg} = 2.4 \times 10^{10} \mathrm{~kg} \mathrm{~m}\) (b) \(\frac{6 \times 10^{6} \mathrm{~m}^{2}}{2 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{~m}^{2}} = \frac{6}{2} \times 10^{6 - (-2)} \mathrm{~m}^{3 - 2} = 3 \times 10^{8} \mathrm{~m}\)  


