## Measurement Using Vernier Callipers 


Suppose, an object is placed between the two jaws, the position of the Vernier scale on the main scale is shown in Fig. 1.3. 


1. Read the main scale marking just infront of zero of the Vernier scale. It shows 4.3 cm. 


2. Find the Vernier scale marking or division which is in line with any of the main scale marking. This shows: 


Length of object = Main scale reading + (Least count × Vernier scale reading). 


\[= 4.3 + 0.01 \times 4 = 4.34 \text{ cm}\]


3. Checking for zero error. Following are some important points to keep in mind before checking zero error: 


(a) If on joining the jaws A and B, the zeros of the main scale and Vernier scale do not exactly coincide with each other then there is an error in the instrument called zero error. 

