## For example:  


(i) Round off to 2 significant figures: \(4.45 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) . (ii) Round off to 2 significant figures: \(4.55 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) . Answer: \(4.4 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) . Answer: \(4.6 \times 10^2 \text{m}\)  


Sometimes, logic is applied to decide the fate of a digit. If we round off to 2 significant figures \(4.452 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) , the answer should be \(4.5 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) since \(4.452 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) is more closer to \(4.5 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) than \(4.4 \times 10^2 \text{m}\) .  


