## Uniform and Non-uniform Velocity  


The velocity is said to be uniform if the speed and direction of a moving body does not change. If the speed or direction or both of them change, it is known as variable velocity or non- uniform velocity.  


Practically, a vehicle does not move in a straight line throughout its journey. It changes its speed or its direction frequently. The example of a body moving with uniform velocity is the downward motion of a  

