================================================================================

\[\text{Average acceleration} = \frac{\text{Change in velocity}}{\text{Time taken}}\]  


\[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{av}} = \frac{\mathbf{v}_t - \mathbf{v}_i}{t}\dots \dots \dots \dots \dots \dots \dots \dots \dots \dots \dots (2.3)\]  


Equation (2.3) can be written as \(\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{av}} = \frac{\Delta\mathbf{v}}{t}\)  


The SI unit of acceleration is \(\mathrm{m s}^{- 2}\)  


If acceleration \(a\) is constant, then Eq 2.3 can be written as: \(\mathbf{v}_f = \mathbf{v}_i + a t\)  


## Uniform and Non-uniform Acceleration  


If time rate of change of velocity is constant, the acceleration is said to be uniform.  


