## Relativity  


In 1905, famous scientist Albert Einstein proposed his revolutionary theory of special relativity which modified many of the basic concepts of physics. According to this theory, speed of light is a universal constant. Its value is approximately \(3 \times 10^{8} \mathrm{~m} \mathrm{~s}^{- 1}\) . Speed of light remains the same for all motions. Any object with mass cannot achieve speeds equal to or greater than that of light. This is known as universal speed limit.  


