## Force Meter  


A force meter is a scientific instrument that measures force. It is also called as a newton meter or a spring balance (Fig.3.19). Now- a- days digital force meters are also available. You have already learnt about mechanical and electronic balances. They measure mass of the objects in kilograms or its multiples. On the other hand, force meter measures force directly in newtons (N).  


An ordinary force meter has a spring inside it. Upper end of the spring is attached to a handle. A hook is attached to the lower end the spring that holds the object. A pointer is also attached to the spring at its upper end. A scale in newtons is provided along the spring such that the pointer coincides with zero of the scale when nothing is hung with the hook.  


