<center>Fig. 3.21 Rubbing hands </center>  


Shooting of stars seen in the sky at night also happen due to friction of air. These are actually asteroids that enter the Earth's atmosphere. As they are moving, air resistance causes generation of heat. Their temperature becomes so high that they start burning and ultimately disintegrate.  


