when you do work pushing a swing, chemical energy in your body is transferred to the swing and appears as energy of the motion of the swing.  


Like work, energy is a scalar quantity. Its SI unit is joule (J).  


When one joule work is done on a body, the amount of energy spent is one joule.  


There are many forms of energy. Electrical energy, chemical energy, nuclear energy, heat energy and light energy are some well- known forms which we shall study later on. There are two basic forms of energy:  


(i) Kinetic energy (ii) Potential energy  


The combination of these two types of energies is called mechanical energy.  


## Kinetic Energy  


The kinetic energy of a body is the energy that a body possesses by virtue of its motion.  


To find out how much kinetic energy a moving body possesses, an opposite force can be applied on the body to stop its motion. Then the work done by the force will be equal to the kinetic energy of the body. i.e., Kinetic energy \((E_{k}) = \text{Work done} (W)\)  


Suppose a body of mass \(m\) is moving with velocity \(v\) . An opposing force \(F\) acting on the body through a distance \(S\) brings it to rest. Then,

