A 1000 kg car moving with an acceleration of \(4\mathrm{m s}^{- 2}\) covers a distance of \(50\mathrm{m}\) in 5 seconds. What is the power generated by its engine?  


## Solution  


Mass of car \(m = 1000\mathrm{kg}\) Acceleration \(a = 4\mathrm{m s}^{- 2}\) Distance \(S = 50\mathrm{m}\) Time taken \(t = 5\mathrm{s}\) Power \(P = ?\)  


First, we shall determine the force applied by Newton's second law.  


\[F = ma = 1000\mathrm{kg}\times 4\mathrm{m}\mathrm{s}^{-2} = 4000\mathrm{N}\]  


From Eq. (5.1), Work, \(W = FS\)  


Or \(W = 4000\mathrm{N}\times 50\mathrm{m} = 2.0\times 10^{5}\mathrm{J}\)  


From Eq. (5.5), \(P = \frac{W}{t}\)  


Putting the values of \(W\) and \(t\) , we have  


\[P = \frac{2.0\times 10^{5}\mathrm{J}}{5\mathrm{s}} = 4\times 10^{4}\mathrm{W} = 40\mathrm{kW}\]  


