equally to all the larger pistons of other cylinders. This pressure causes these pistons to move outward pressing the brake pads towards brake discs or brake drums. Force of friction between the pads and discs or drums slows down the vehicle. When pressure is released from the pedal, the springs pull back the brake pads and wheels again turn freely.  


