## Plasma  


The plasma is a gas in which most of the atoms are ionized containing positive ions and electrons (Fig. 7.3- a). They are freely moving in the volume of the gas. Due to presence of positive ions and free electrons, plasma is the conducting state of matter. It allows electric current to pass through it. Since the gas in plasma state has properties which are quite different from ordinary gas, therefore, plasma is known as fourth  

