state of matter. The Sun and the most of other stars are in plasma state. Plasma is also found in plasma TV and in gas discharge tubes (Fig. 7.3- b) when electric current passes through them. The plasma state also occurs during the early stages of lightning formation known as lightning streamers which are the conducting paths through the atmosphere due to ionized air molecules.  

