## 4. Is Isolated Magnetic Pole Possible?  


If we break a bar magnet into two equal pieces, can we get N- pole and S- pole separately? No, it is not possible. Each piece will have its two poles, i.e., N- pole and S- pole. Even if a magnet is divided into thousands pieces, each piece will be a complete magnet with its N, and S- poles (Fig.8.6).  

