## 1. Observation  


1. ObservationThe first step in scientific method is to make observations of natural processes and to collect the data about them. This may be done either by ordinary observations or by obtaining the results from different experiments. For example, it is our common observation that shadow of an opaque object is formed when it is placed in the path of light coming from the Sun or a lamp (Fig.9.1).  

