## 3. Experiment  


Experiment is an organized repeatable process which is used to test the truth of a hypothesis.  


To verify the assumption made in the above example, four cardboards, each with a hole, are placed in a straight line, such that the hole in \(1^{\text{st}}\) card is in front of a torch. When we see through the hole in cards, we can see the light of the torch (Fig. 9.2- a). If any of these cards is displaced, we cannot see light passing through (Fig. 9.2- b). Thus, this experiment proves that light travels in a straight line.  

