After the successful verification of an assumption and with the help of careful experimentation, it becomes a theory and is applicable to similar phenomena. With the help of the above experiment, the assumption has been proved that light travels in a straight line. So, it then becomes a theory.  


It is a logical explanation of the causes and effects of an issue or an event that occurs in nature.  

