Plasma: A state of matter in which most of the atoms are ionized into positive ions and electrons.  


Power: Rate of doing work.  


Precision: Determined by the instrument used equal to its least count.  


Prefix: Symbols added to a unit to write it by power of 10.  


Pressure: Force exerted normally on unit area of an object.  


Random Motion: Motion without any consideration of time and direction.  


